// The disk's thickness: a thin sheet of particles overall, but noticeably
// thicker near the core (y_thickness falls linearly from 300 milli-units at
// r=0 to 60 at (import maximum_radius)), with the actual vertical offset a PRNG
// sample in -thickness..+thickness (noise_range, scene/math/rng/lset.id).

particle_y(int radius) {
  int thick = y_thickness(radius);
  int vertical_offset = noise_range(thick);
} return int vertical_offset;
given initialize_math (0):(-151)
given initialize_math (5000):(-23)

y_thickness(int radius) {
  int thickness_amount = 300 - radius * 240 / (import maximum_radius);
} return int thickness_amount;
(0):(300)
(5000):(60)
